<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pondicherry</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Puducherry</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pondicherry, officially Puducherry, is a coastal city in south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chennai">Chennai</a>. Founded as a French trading post by François Martin in 1674, it became the capital of French India and, under Dupleix in the 1740s, the base of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>'s bid for power in southern India. It was transferred to India in 1954 and is the capital of the Union Territory of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/puducherry-union-territory">Puducherry</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pondicherry.jpg" alt="Pondicherry" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Karthik Easvur · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pondicherry-Rock_beach_aerial_view.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
